---
description: Conventions for run.sh, installer.sh and scripts/
globs: "{*.sh,scripts/**}"
alwaysApply: false
---

# Shell scripts

- Bash with `set -euo pipefail`; they must work with macOS's bash 3.2 (no `mapfile`, no `${var,,}`, no
  associative arrays).
- Shared helpers (colours, `die`, `note`, `ask`, `ensure_node`, `ensure_packages`) live in `scripts/common.sh`;
  scripts set `MANAGER_DIR` and `source` it.
- `run.sh` loops on exit code 75 (the manager restarting after an update) and exports `MANAGER_RESTART=1`;
  keep that loop when editing it.
- Packages install with `npm ci` when `package-lock.json` exists, so a git clone stays clean for updates.
- Prompts must have a default and work without a TTY (`--yes`, piped input).
- Never touch anything outside the manager folder and the workspace the user chose; never `sudo`.
- Check syntax after editing: `bash -n run.sh installer.sh scripts/common.sh`.
- Test `installer.sh` only on a copy under `/tmp` (`rsync` the repo without `.cache`, `.git`), never in a real
  install.
